using Global

~ flashback_start

# Setting: Six months ago. A private meeting room. Volkov, a returning buyer, wants to escalate the deal beyond software licensing.

Volkov: The targeting software works well. My people are pleased.

Volkov: Now I want the hardware interface. The part that lets it talk directly to a weapons platform.

Jason: That's not something we sell. Not to anyone. Not even to you.

Volkov: Everything is something you sell, Jason. We both know that by now.

- Hold the line, no exceptions. [if leverage >= 0]
	Jason: The software's the deal. It's the only deal. If that's not enough, we're done here.
	do leverage += 1
	do compliance -= 1
	=> volkov_held_line

- Offer a smaller compromise. [if compliance >= 0]
	Jason: I can get you an expanded license — more units, priority support. Not the hardware interface. That's a line I won't cross.
	do compliance += 1
	=> volkov_compromise

- Consider it, quietly.
	Jason: Let me see what's actually possible. I'm not promising anything.
	do leverage -= 1
	do compliance += 1
	=> volkov_considered

~ volkov_held_line

Volkov: (studies him for a long moment) Interesting. You have limits after all.

Volkov: Fine. The software, expanded terms. We'll revisit the rest another time.

Jason: (There wouldn't be another time. Jason already knew that. He just hadn't said it yet.)

do Global.volkov_path = "held_line"

=> buyer_returns_end

~ volkov_compromise

Volkov: Acceptable. For now.

Jason: (For now. Volkov's favorite phrase. It always meant the conversation wasn't over.)

do Global.volkov_path = "compromise"

=> buyer_returns_end

~ volkov_considered

Volkov: Good. I like people who understand that "no" is rarely permanent.

Jason: (He hadn't said yes. He also hadn't said no. He was starting to understand that was its own kind of answer.)

do compliance -= 1
do Global.volkov_path = "considered"

=> buyer_returns_end

~ buyer_returns_end

Jason: (Driving home that night, Jason understood, for the first time clearly, that this didn't have a ceiling. He started drafting his resignation letter that weekend.)

do Global.return_from_flashback()

=> END
